# Server-side settings for the backend AND the pdf-service (roadmap step 7a).
#
#   cp .env.example .env        # .env is git-ignored
#
# ONE file for both, on purpose: they need the same AUTH0_DOMAIN and
# AUTH0_AUDIENCE, and a mismatch between them shows up as a 401 with no useful
# message. The frontend is configured separately, in
# Web App/frontend/.env.local — Vite only exposes variables prefixed VITE_, and
# only reads files inside its own project.
#
# A real exported environment variable always beats this file, so a deployment
# that sets them properly ignores whatever is here.
#
# Leave AUTH0_DOMAIN and AUTH0_AUDIENCE blank and both services run in BYPASS
# mode: no real login, a warning banner at startup, and `/api/health` reporting
# "authBypass": true. That is the intended state until an Auth0 tenant exists.
#
# Full walkthrough: Web App/docs/auth_spec.md §3.

# Auth0 Dashboard -> Applications -> your SPA -> Settings -> Domain
AUTH0_DOMAIN=
# Auth0 Dashboard -> Applications -> APIs -> your API -> Identifier.
# Must be byte-identical to VITE_AUTH0_AUDIENCE in the frontend's .env.local.
AUTH0_AUDIENCE=

# This address becomes an `admin` the first time it signs in — the only way to
# create the first one before step 7f ships an admin screen. Applied on account
# creation only, so it cannot re-promote someone who was later demoted.
BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_EMAIL=

# --- rarely changed ------------------------------------------------------

# `production` forbids the auth bypass entirely and makes AUTH0_DOMAIN,
# AUTH0_AUDIENCE and CORS_ORIGINS mandatory — the services refuse to start
# without them rather than quietly running unauthenticated.
# APP_ENV=development

# Force the bypass back on while Auth0 IS configured. This is what the
# browser-driven checks in scripts/ need, because Google and Auth0's hosted
# login both block automated sign-in. Ignored when APP_ENV=production.
# DEV_AUTH_BYPASS=1

# Defaults to a SQLite file at Web App/backend/maze_studio.db. Point it at
# Postgres for deployment; the schema and migrations are engine-neutral.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://user:pass@host/maze_studio

# Comma-separated browser origins allowed to call the API. Defaults to the Vite
# dev servers. REQUIRED when APP_ENV=production.
# CORS_ORIGINS=https://maze-studio.example
